"id":"euler.lemma-2.5","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2.5","locator":"Lemma 2.5, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2.5.** Let $0<\\varepsilon\\le1$. The solution $Y$ of (2.12) exists for all $\\tau\\ge0$, satisfies $|Y|\\le1$, and has the form $$\\begin{equation}\n Y=(1+e)\\cos\\varphi-\\tfrac14\\varepsilon\\tau\\sin2\\varphi,\n \\qquad 0\\le e\\le\\tfrac18\\varepsilon. \\tag{2.13}\n\\end{equation}$$ The reference amplitude satisfies $$\\begin{equation}\n a_{\\rm ref}(\\tau)=\\sqrt{\\cos\\varphi(\\tau)}\n       \\exp\\left(\\int_0^\\tau(1+e)\\cos\\varphi\\,d\\tau'\\right). \\tag{2.14}\n\\end{equation}$$ The function $Y$ has exactly one zero $\\tau_m$, with $2\\le\\varepsilon\\tau_m\\le3$. It is positive before this zero and negative afterwards, so $a_{\\rm ref}$ is largest at $\\tau_m$, and $$\\log a_{\\rm ref}(\\tau_m)\\ge\\varepsilon^{-1/2}-1.$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.5","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.5","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.5%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_2_5%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.5%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_2_5%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/lean.TorusEuler.Paper.Statement.lemma_2_5"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.5","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.5%22%2C%22lean.TorusEuler.Pape